-- KG_LOUVAIN_GRAPH.hdbprocedure
-- ============================================================
-- TEMPORARY DEPLOY-UNBLOCK STUB — issue #917 follow-up
--
-- The GraphScript body originally shipped with #984 fails HDI
-- precompile with:
--
--   Error: com.sap.hana.di.procedure: Syntax error:
--     "exception 73002201: syntax error, unexpected AS,
--      expecting FOREACH or "," near "AS"" [8250009]
--     at "src/procedures/KG_LOUVAIN_GRAPH.hdbprocedure" (57:36)
--
-- The `o_members = SELECT ... AS ... FROM :communities JOIN ...`
-- projection is not legal GraphScript — the language expects a
-- FOREACH iteration over MULTISET members, not a SQL-style JOIN
-- projection. Getting the correct GraphScript idiom right requires
-- a probe against real HANA Cloud (there is no dry-run for
-- GraphScript syntax outside HDI make), which is not something
-- we want to iterate on at 22:00 the night Tom needs a working DEV.
--
-- This stub returns an empty result set with the same shape. The
-- downstream contract in srv/jobs/kg-communities-job.js is fail-
-- open: an empty procedure result → `KgCommunity` sidecar left
-- empty → admin FE `/admin-ui/#kgCommunities` renders "No data"
-- rather than a 500. That's the same fallback path already used
-- for the nightly job's own exception paths, so no new behavior
-- degradation.
--
-- Everything else in tonight's merges (#988 homepage personalization,
-- #987 KG WCC isolation, #916 PageRank ranking) is unaffected — the
-- only functional gap is that Louvain community memberships won't
-- populate. That surface is DEV-only in v1 per the #917 spec, so
-- production is not impacted.
--
-- REMOVAL:
--   Restore the intended GraphScript body once the correct
--   iteration form has been probed against DEV HANA Cloud. See
--   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-04-917-kg-community-detection-
--   design.md and the HANA docs sample referenced in the sibling
--   KG_SHORTEST_PATH_GRAPH.hdbprocedure (`FOREACH v IN Vertices(:p)
--   WITH ORDINALITY AS <name>`).
--
-- Spec:  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-04-917-kg-community-detection-design.md
-- Issue: #917
-- ============================================================

PROCEDURE KG_LOUVAIN_GRAPH (
  OUT o_members TABLE (
    community_id BIGINT,
    vertex_key   NVARCHAR(280),
    vertex_type  NVARCHAR(16),
    slug         NVARCHAR(255)
  )
)
LANGUAGE SQLSCRIPT SQL SECURITY INVOKER READS SQL DATA AS
BEGIN
  -- Return an empty result set with the declared shape. See header
  -- for the deploy-unblock rationale.
  o_members = SELECT CAST(NULL AS BIGINT)          AS community_id,
                     CAST(NULL AS NVARCHAR(280))   AS vertex_key,
                     CAST(NULL AS NVARCHAR(16))    AS vertex_type,
                     CAST(NULL AS NVARCHAR(255))   AS slug
              FROM DUMMY
              WHERE 1 = 0;
END;
